From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] gtk4: expose native Activity Manager section

The ISO ships an Activity Manager only in its GTK3 extension tree. Register the
GTK4 overlay section explicitly so Settings exposes the inventory without
mixing GTK3 modules into the modern process.

--- a/src/jarabe/controlpanel/gui.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/controlpanel/gui.py
@@ -447,4 +447,17 @@
                 except Exception:
                     logging.exception('Exception while loading extension:')

+        try:
+            import cpsection.activities
+            options.setdefault('activities', {
+                'alerts': [],
+                'view': 'ActivityManager',
+                'icon': cpsection.activities.ICON,
+                'title': cpsection.activities.TITLE,
+                'color': None,
+                'keywords': list(cpsection.activities.KEYWORDS),
+            })
+        except Exception:
+            logging.exception('Exception while loading GTK4 Activity Manager:')
+
         return options
